# SECTION 0 — MISSION AND NON-NEGOTIABLE PRINCIPLES

## 0.1 Mission

Implement a continuous improvement system that transforms verified operational experience into controlled improvements of ASR models.

The platform must continuously:

1. Observe production inference behavior.
2. Detect potentially incorrect transcriptions.
3. Identify changes in input audio distributions.
4. Identify language-specific weaknesses.
5. Detect new and recurring vocabulary problems.
6. Identify difficult acoustic conditions.
7. Discover model regressions.
8. Collect eligible user corrections.
9. Select high-value samples for human review.
10. Produce verified reference transcripts.
11. Construct new training datasets.
12. Train new candidate models.
13. Evaluate candidate models against immutable benchmarks.
14. Promote only validated models.
15. Monitor production performance after deployment.
16. Roll back degraded releases.

The ultimate objective is to improve:

- Persian CER.
- English CER.
- Mixed-language CER.
- Conversational Persian.
- Proper-noun recognition.
- Technical terminology.
- Noisy-speech robustness.
- Native Streaming stability.
- Long-form transcription consistency.
- Model inference efficiency.

## 0.2 Critical learning prohibition

The system must never automatically treat an ASR output as ground truth.

The following are distinct records:

1. Original audio.
2. Original ASR hypothesis.
3. User-submitted correction.
4. Human-reviewed transcript.
5. Adjudicated reference transcript.
6. Approved training label.

They must never be silently merged.

A user correction may be incomplete, mistaken or intentionally manipulated.

A second model output may also be incorrect.

Two models agreeing does not establish that their shared output is correct.

Only an approved reference-generation workflow may promote a transcription to verified training ground truth.

## 0.3 No unrestricted online weight updates

Do not modify production model weights directly from individual user requests.

Do not update a live model after every corrected sentence.

Do not continuously train on unreviewed production transcripts.

All new model weights must pass a versioned training and release pipeline.

Production learning is an offline controlled process.

## 0.4 Separation of responsibilities

The following systems must remain independent:

- Production inference.
- Feedback collection.
- Annotation.
- Dataset construction.
- Model training.
- Model evaluation.
- Model release.

A production inference request must not automatically trigger an expensive training process.

The Feedback Service may generate candidate learning records, but only authorized workflows may promote them into training datasets.

