## 1.2 Core services

Implement the following services.

### A. Production Feedback Collector

Captures eligible user corrections and quality feedback.

### B. Consent and Data Eligibility Gate

Determines whether audio, transcript and associated metadata are permitted for research and training.

### C. Production Error Intelligence

Identifies recurring failure patterns and potential model weaknesses.

### D. Active Learning Selector

Selects samples with high potential research value.

### E. Annotation Management System

Assigns samples to qualified human annotators.

### F. Adjudication Engine

Resolves disagreements and creates approved reference transcripts.

### G. Training Data Builder

Creates reproducible training dataset releases.

### H. Dataset Lineage Manager

Tracks sample origins, transformations, licenses and training usage.

### I. Continuous Training Orchestrator

Creates controlled model-training experiments.

### J. Model Evaluation Gate

Measures whether a new checkpoint provides a real improvement.

### K. Model Release Controller

Controls model promotion and deployment.

### L. Production Drift Detector

Detects changes in input distribution and measured performance.

### M. Rollback Controller

Restores the last approved model or routing policy when defined failure conditions occur.

## 1.3 Architecture isolation requirements

The following boundaries are mandatory:

- Feedback Service must not have unrestricted access to model weights.
- Annotation Service must not have production model deployment permissions.
- Training workers must not access production secrets.
- Production inference must not read mutable training manifests.
- Model Release Controller must not publish an unverified checkpoint.
- Dataset Builder must enforce all consent and license rules.
- Policy Optimizer must not update active production policy directly.

All component interactions must use documented APIs or approved message contracts.

