   |
   +------> REJECTED
   |
   v
PROMOTION_REVIEW
   |
   v
RELEASE_CANDIDATE
```

A training job may be cancelled at any stage before release.

## 10.6 Scheduler policy

The scheduler must support:

- Priority.
- Compute availability.
- GPU type.
- Estimated duration.
- Cost ceiling.
- Dataset dependency.
- Model dependency.
- Concurrency limit.
- Cancellation.
- Retry.
- Checkpoint resume.

Production inference workloads have priority over nonurgent research training unless infrastructure has separate reserved capacity.

## 10.7 No automatic budget escalation

Never increase the approved training budget automatically.

If the experiment exceeds its estimate:

- Pause or stop.
- Report the variance.
- Require approval for additional expenditure.

