# SECTION 11 — CONTINUOUS MODEL TRAINING

## 11.1 Model training strategy

Use the Phase 4 model as the primary continued-adaptation baseline.

Training choices may include:

- Fine-tuning.
- LoRA/PEFT where supported.
- Distillation.
- Vocabulary adaptation.
- Noise adaptation.
- Domain adaptation.
- Controlled replay of historic training data.

Do not assume that newly collected data alone is sufficient.

## 11.2 Replay buffer

Maintain a representative historical sample pool.

Its purpose is to prevent catastrophic forgetting of previously supported capabilities.

Initial replay strategy:

- 70% newly approved data.
- 30% historical representative data.

This ratio is a candidate experiment setting.

Evaluate alternatives:

- 90/10.
- 80/20.
- 70/30.
- 50/50.

Historical samples must remain source- and license-eligible.

Do not allow replay data to be drawn from a protected test set.

## 11.3 Catastrophic forgetting evaluation

For every candidate model compare:

- Persian standard.
- Persian conversational.
- English.
- Code-switching.
- Technical vocabulary.
- Noise robustness.
- Long-form speech.

A candidate that improves a new domain but materially degrades an existing language must not be promoted without an explicit product decision.

