# SECTION 23 — PERFORMANCE AND OPERATIONAL LIMITS

## 23.1 Feedback ingestion

Initial objectives:

- Feedback API P95 below 300 ms.
- Idempotent submission.
- No synchronous training execution.
- No synchronous large audio processing on the feedback request thread.

## 23.2 Annotation throughput

Track actual:

- Samples per hour.
- Audio minutes per annotation hour.
- Adjudication percentage.
- Quality rejection rate.
- Cost per approved audio hour.

Do not set fixed annotation productivity targets without a pilot.

## 23.3 Dataset build

Initial objective:

Generate manifests for 100,000 metadata records within 10 minutes on the defined reference worker, excluding full audio decoding.

This is a target to measure, not a claimed capability.

## 23.4 Training scheduling

The learning orchestrator must not interfere with production inference capacity.

Maintain separate resource pools or explicit GPU reservations.

## 23.5 Queue limits

All queues must be bounded.

Separate:

- Feedback ingestion.
- Annotation tasks.
- Dataset building.
- Training jobs.
- Model evaluation.
- Release jobs.

Apply priority and backpressure.

Do not allow a large feedback burst to exhaust resources required for active transcription.

