The system allows unauthorized training, contaminates protected evaluation data, corrupts model provenance or deploys an unverified checkpoint.

A model-training experiment may fail to improve accuracy while the continuous-learning infrastructure itself succeeds, provided the failed experiment is accurately documented.

Never relabel a non-improving candidate as a successful model release.

