# FINAL ENGINEERING COMMAND

The goal is to establish a controlled learning loop that improves the independent ASR engine without contaminating datasets, violating permissions, degrading existing capabilities or destabilizing production.

The system must learn from verified evidence, not from its own unverified predictions.

A large volume of unverified feedback is not a valuable training corpus.

A smaller, diverse, correctly labeled and fully permissioned dataset is more useful than a large dataset with uncertain provenance.

A model that improves Persian while destroying English is not an overall improvement.

A model that improves benchmark CER but causes unacceptable streaming latency is not automatically a better production model.

A model that cannot be reproduced, traced and rolled back must not be promoted.

**Start with Stage 9.0. Audit the real capabilities of the existing platform. Implement feedback and consent controls before active learning. Implement human verification before dataset promotion. Implement dataset versioning before retraining. Implement evaluation before model release.**

Never skip a dependency stage to make the project appear more autonomous.

The final objective is a continuously improving, independent, Persian-English ASR platform with controlled data governance, measurable learning efficiency and safe production model evolution.

